{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall keep themselves separate from the holy offerings of the children of Israel.</b> Lest they think that because of the greatness of their rank, the people's consecrated offerings are as ordinary (חוּלִין) to them — as in the matter of 'one excommunicated against a disciple is not excommunicated against his teacher' (Mo'ed Qatan 16a). <b>And they shall not profane the name of the holy things which they dedicate to Me.</b> They shall not profane the name of that consecrated offering which Israel dedicate to Me, upon which they have called the name of holiness."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:16.106447623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}